<title>GERMANY: World castor oil exports seen down in 1996/97.</title>
<headline>World castor oil exports seen down in 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global castor oil exports are likely to fall to 247,000 tonnes in 1996/97 from 300,000 tonnes in the previous season, the independent Oil World newsletter said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The publication cited production shortfalls in Indian castor seed.</p>
<p>The country accounted for nearly 90 percent of world castor oil exports in calendar 1996.</p>
<p>World castor seed production in 1996/97 was put at 1.17 million tonnes, down from 1.24 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>India's seed output was estimated at 850,000 tonnes from 930,000 tonnes in the previous season.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
